Modifications
=============
This fork includes the following changes relative to `chrono-tz` 0.10.4 /
`chrono-tz-build` 0.5.0 / `parse-zoneinfo` 0.4.0:

- Non-breaking upstream improvements cherry-picked from `chronotope/chrono-tz`:
  - `chrono-tz#211` (Robert Bastian): `%z` numeric offset format support in
    `parse-zoneinfo` (`0.5.0`)
  - `chrono-tz#214` (Robert Bastian): link deduplication in `chrono-tz-build`
  - `chrono-tz#218` (Robert Bastian): fix regex filtering (`CHRONO_TZ_TIMEZONE_FILTER`)
    to stop pulling in unrelated `Etc/GMT*` and `UTC` zones (`chrono-tz#215`)
  - `chrono-tz#222` (Dirkjan Ochtman): lifetime elision warning cleanups in
    `parse-zoneinfo`
  - `chrono-tz#223` (Yotam Ofek): update `phf` / `phf_codegen` / `phf_shared`
    to `0.13`
  - `chrono-tz#224` (Yotam Ofek): depend on `serde_core` instead of `serde`
  - `chrono-tz#225` (Yotam Ofek): bump MSRV to Rust 1.66.0 across all crates
  - `chrono-tz#226` (Paul Bender): feature-gated `defmt` (`1.0.1`) support
  - `chrono-tz#227` (Paul Bender): clippy warning fixes in `chrono-tz-build`
- IANA Time Zone Database updated from `2025b` to `2026f`
- Security and robustness fixes by the Sadco Security Team:
  - `sad-parse-zoneinfo`: O(1) checked Gregorian year-to-timestamp calculation
    replacing the O(|year - 1970|) loop; checked day/weekday/time parsing and
    calendar math without panics or integer wrap/overflow; graceful handling of
    `Year::Minimum` / `Year::Maximum`; cycle-safe link resolution and validation
    for broken links and missing continuation rulesets; safe `%z` formatting for
    fractional-minute offsets and extreme values; panic-free transition table
    generation with checked/saturating arithmetic; inline `#` comment `break` fix;
    and safe handling of `>= 4`-segment zone names in `structure.rs`
  - `sad-chrono-tz-build`: transitive cycle-safe link resolution, build-time
    validation of `FixedTimespan` offsets (`i32` and `|offset| < 86_400`),
    escaped string emission in generated Rust code, and filtered 3-level
    submodule trees
  - `sad-chrono-tz`: saturating arithmetic in `FixedTimespanSet::local_span`,
    bounded untrusted input length in `SerdeError`, and target dependency on
    `sad-chrono 0.4` (`0.4.46+`)
- Packaging and governance:
  - Published as `sad-chrono-tz` (`0.10.5`, library `sad_chrono_tz`),
    `sad-chrono-tz-build` (`0.5.1`, library `sad_chrono_tz_build`), and
    `sad-parse-zoneinfo` (`0.5.1`, library `sad_parse_zoneinfo`)
  - Real `LICENSE-MIT` and `LICENSE-APACHE` files replacing symlinks

The upstream fixes listed above were written by their upstream authors; see
CHANGELOG.md for attribution of each change. The packaging changes and the
Sadco Security Team fixes listed above were developed by the Sadco Security Team
with assistance from AI coding tools (Anthropic Claude, Google Gemini).
